WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.629 --> 00:00:11.099
We told you in a previous video about how
Saudi Arabia wants to leave behind, once and

00:00:11.099 --> 00:00:16.420
for all, its addiction to oil, and become
a nation similar to Dubai or Abu Dhabi.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:20.580
In this video, we’re going to look at this
country in more depth in order to get an idea

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:29.070
of how this mission to get free from oil is
going.

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:34.520
The thing is there is a specific name, a leader
behind this ambitious plan.

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:36.829
Do you know who this person is?

00:00:36.829 --> 00:00:42.410
Well, for those of you who don't, the person
who is turning everything upside down is Mohamed

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:44.550
Bin Salman.

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:48.301
&nbsp;
But a name alone doesn't explain much, so

00:00:48.301 --> 00:00:51.130
now you might be wondering: Who is this man
really?

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:52.640
What are his intentions?

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:54.810
And what exactly is he trying to do?

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:59.120
Well, these are the questions we are going
to be answering in today’s Visual Politik

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:00.120
video…

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.890
So let’s get going shall we?

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:05.720
THE PRINCE OF CHANGE

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:11.140
He might be only a little more than 30 years
old, but Mohamed Bin Salman is already one

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:16.549
of the most powerful people in the world and
he controls more money than we could ever

00:01:16.549 --> 00:01:17.789
possibly count.

00:01:17.789 --> 00:01:22.369
Formally, he is Minister of Defense, Deputy
Crown Prince, Second Deputy Prime Minister,

00:01:22.369 --> 00:01:27.009
Chief of the Royal Court and Chair of the
Council for Economic and Development Affairs...

00:01:27.009 --> 00:01:29.340
So what does all of that mean?

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:35.469
Well, it kind of means that Mohamed Bin Salman
is in control of everything…

00:01:35.469 --> 00:01:40.009
He's got complete control over the country’s
oil, over the massive financial reserves that

00:01:40.009 --> 00:01:44.500
have been accumulated over the years and,
also, over Saudi Arabia’s massive defence

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:45.500
budget.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:49.129
So, today, the power of the prince is practically
total.

00:01:49.129 --> 00:01:52.640
&nbsp;
And, hey, this isn't something normal.

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:55.950
Never has such a young man had so much power
before.

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:59.799
Up until now, the norm was for the country
to be controlled by seniors of 80 years or

00:01:59.799 --> 00:02:04.479
more who were very reluctant for any kind
of change.

00:02:04.479 --> 00:02:08.009
But all of a sudden, change is underfoot,
because what Mohammed Bin Salman is trying

00:02:08.009 --> 00:02:13.460
to do with Saudi Arabia is to turn it into
a new United Arab Emirates, a country which

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:16.750
the prince has an enormous amount of admiration
for.

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:20.060
Later, we are going to see just how he is
doing this, but for now, you need to bear

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:21.220
something in mind:

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:26.000
The youth of the country cheer Bin Salman
as the savior of the Kingdom.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:32.640
And this is a country where half of its population
is less than 25 years old so, well, that is

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:33.730
pretty important.

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:36.920
But, now you might be wondering: Where does
this man come from?

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:39.380
How can such a young man have so much power?

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:44.860
Well… he is the son of the current King.

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:46.940
But wait a second before you exclaim: “Well!

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:48.530
Of course he is!”

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:53.870
You do need to know that being the son of
the king in Saudi Arabia wasn't such an important

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:59.400
thing, in fact, for now, Bin Salman is not
even the heir of the Saudi throne...

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:03.450
THE BATTLE OVER THE THRONE

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:08.220
Salman bin Abdulaziz is the king of Saudi
Arabia, he is the son of the man who is considered

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:11.330
the founder of the country: Abdulaziz Bin
Saud.

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:16.880
Well, since Saud died in 1953, the kingdom
has been inherited by brother after brother.

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:22.790
AUDIO: (Abdulaziz Bin Saud had 17 known wives
and it is calculated that he also had around

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:24.290
32 sons.

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:26.840
So there were quite a few potential heirs).

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:30.410
The thing is that, when the current king,
who is believed to be the 25th son, reached

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:36.140
power a few years ago in 2015, the first thing
he did was to change the laws of succession.

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:39.720
Even though some of his brothers are still
alive, he has decided to put the new generations

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:41.250
in charge of the succession.

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:45.660
To do this, he decided to appoint his nephew,
Mohammed Bin Nayef, who is closer to Washington

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:49.680
than others, and he has been in charge for
security in the last years, as well as the

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:52.189
secret services and the fight against fundamentalism.

00:03:52.189 --> 00:03:56.260
&nbsp;
However, it seems like young Mohammed Bin

00:03:56.260 --> 00:04:00.790
Salman, the main character in this video,
is not very happy about that, and it seems

00:04:00.790 --> 00:04:03.080
that he is taking aim at the throne…

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:05.260
He wants to become the future king of Saudi
Arabia.

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:07.740
&nbsp;
So, his eagerness for reforms could be explained

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:09.760
as an attempt to gain popularity.

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:12.170
That is what most analysts think.

00:04:12.170 --> 00:04:15.350
And it does make sense.

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:19.250
The fall of the prices in oil has given Mohammed
Bin Salman the opportunity to aim for the

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:22.030
throne, which is something his father obviously
supports.

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:24.810
&nbsp;
If Saudi Vision 2030 starts showing good results,

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:29.320
Bin Salman will be in a better position to
ask for a reward, and become, potentially,

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:30.440
the new heir to the throne.

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:33.350
&nbsp;
However, there are a few problems on the road

00:04:33.350 --> 00:04:35.760
ahead, both for Bin Salman as well as for
the country.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:37.490
&nbsp;
On the one hand, there are problems inside

00:04:37.490 --> 00:04:42.320
the royal family: Bin Salman has made a lot
of enemies who accuse him of being power hungry.

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:46.560
On the other hand, his father, the current
king, is quite old (81) and he seems to have

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:48.580
some memory issues.

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:52.290
So this means there are two possible scenarios
ahead:

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:54.370
&nbsp;
If the current king lives for many more years,

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:57.300
the prince, Bin Salman will be able to consolidate
his power.

00:04:57.300 --> 00:05:00.960
However, if the king doesn’t live so long,
the current heir, Bin Salman’s cousin, could

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:08.570
become the new king and wish goodbye both
to the prince and his Saudi Vision 2030 vision.

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:12.120
But that is how these monarchies work…

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:16.380
But I am sure that some of you are thinking
by now: Well, this is all fascinating Simon,

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:18.889
but why should I care about what happens in
Saudi Arabia?

00:05:18.889 --> 00:05:22.280
Well, you should care, and probably more than
you might think.

00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:28.070
Saudi Arabia is still the biggest oil producer
and it is also the most important and influential

00:05:28.070 --> 00:05:31.210
country in the Arab world.

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:39.320
An evolution towards openness for this country
could be something very positive for the world,

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:44.090
and for now, the planned Saudi Vision 2030
seems to be the only opportunity for the country

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:46.010
to progress and evolve.

00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:54.860
But, now that we’ve said that, what exactly
is the plan for this country?

00:05:54.860 --> 00:05:57.430
INCORRIGIBLES

00:05:57.430 --> 00:06:01.310
So far in today’s story, we have seen a
handsome prince and a battle over the throne...

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:07.430
But we need a third ingredient for this Saudi
soap opera: luxury and money...

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:11.990
Well, of all the royal families in the world,
the Sauds, the royal household of Saudi Arabia

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:14.810
might be the most addicted to money and luxury.

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:17.120
And now you are going to see why...

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:18.650
We have mentioned it in several videos...

00:06:18.650 --> 00:06:23.320
The fall of oil prices has jeopardised many
countries and, among them, is Saudi Arabia.

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:28.900
AUDIO: (Only in 2016, and even though many
adjustments were made, the country had a deficit

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:31.400
of more than 80 billion dollars…).

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:37.790
And now the question becomes: What can they
do in order to fix such a hole in their budget?

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:41.850
Well, in 2016, the Saudi Government announced
the country would go on a diet.

00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:45.690
So, for the first time in decades, austerity
reached Saudi Arabia.

00:06:45.690 --> 00:06:50.960
AUDIO: (The government of Bin Salman started
with reductions in public wages, cancelled

00:06:50.960 --> 00:07:04.009
many projects whose profitability was uncertain,
reduced subsidies on gasoline, water, electricity…)

00:07:04.009 --> 00:07:08.540
&nbsp;
This was a pretty huge shock for one of the

00:07:08.540 --> 00:07:10.780
most subsidized economies in the world.

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:15.460
I mean, up until now, dear viewer, oil had
helped to pay for everything in Saudi Arabia.

00:07:15.460 --> 00:07:18.910
However, hold on for just a minute, because
that is not the whole story...

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:23.630
AUDIO: (“Under Salman´s rule, princes still
enjoy many material privileges.

00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:26.730
The subsidization system hasn't changed for
the Royal Household”.

00:07:26.730 --> 00:07:28.080
Steffen Hertog, London School of Economics.)

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:33.570
Take a look at this, the king of Saudi Arabia
has ultra-luxurious palaces all over the world

00:07:33.570 --> 00:07:34.600
available to him.

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:39.400
In Marbella in Spain, he has “ El Rocío”,
a palace inspired by no less than the White

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:40.400
House.

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:45.490
&nbsp;
But, I mean, it’s gotta be pretty boring

00:07:45.490 --> 00:07:48.230
to have to go to the same palace all the time
right?

00:07:48.230 --> 00:07:49.230
How tiresome!

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:53.240
So, last summer, the king built a new and
gigantic palace in Tangier, Morocco.

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:58.040
The palace has its very own hospital and,
here, the king gets French seafood delivered

00:07:58.040 --> 00:07:59.300
direct from France.

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:00.300
http://www.dailymail.co.uk/news/article-4069078/Saudi-s-King-Salman-lavishes-MILLIONS-Moroccan-hideaway-including-helicopter-pads-tent-size-circus-big-top.html

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:03.720
But hey, what’s the problem with chartering
a few airplanes so the king can eat some nice

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:04.889
lobsters, right?

00:08:04.889 --> 00:08:09.060
Oh, and when the king of Saudi Arabia travels…he
travels big!

00:08:09.060 --> 00:08:15.090
AUDIO: (In his last tour around Asia, in 2016,
the king travelled with 1500 people, &nbsp;&nbsp;luggage

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:19.990
weighed 459 tons and he took with him two
Mercedes-Benz S600 limos.

00:08:19.990 --> 00:08:23.550
In order to carry it all 27 planes had to
be used).

00:08:23.550 --> 00:08:26.259
&nbsp;
Yes, so it seems this is what the royal family

00:08:26.259 --> 00:08:28.050
considers austerity.

00:08:28.050 --> 00:08:29.050
&nbsp;
And the prince Mohamed Bin Salman, our main

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:31.400
character in today’s video, is no different:

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:35.720
AUDIO: (During some holidays in France and
at the same time the prices in oil were falling,

00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:39.220
the prince Salman saw the yacht of the Russian
magnate Yuri Shefler.

00:08:39.220 --> 00:08:40.770
It was love at first sight.

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:45.800
He sent an assistant right away in order to
close the deal: Salman bought it for 550 million

00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:46.800
dollars).

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:47.800
https://megaricos.com/2016/10/20/el-principe-saudi-mohammed-bin-salman-compro-el-mega-yate-serene-por-e500-millones/
&nbsp;

00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:53.390
So, now know how the family likes to live,
and they are quite a big family.

00:08:53.390 --> 00:08:58.190
Some estimations indicate the Saudi royal
family has around 15,000 members.

00:08:58.190 --> 00:09:02.180
The government has evaded the question of
membership numbers, but even low end estimates

00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:04.430
put it at about 5,000 people.

00:09:04.430 --> 00:09:08.640
And we are talking about people who live thanks
to the public budget and have all kinds of

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:14.170
privileges: they are paid impressive salaries,
they have access to hospitals which are essentially

00:09:14.170 --> 00:09:17.240
palaces with 5-star hotel services, and they
do profitable business with the government.

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:22.690
They have incredibly luxurious and rather
incredible lifestyles.

00:09:22.690 --> 00:09:26.000
And that is very, very expensive.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:30.100
According to estimations from the US government,
since transparency is not a tradition in the

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:35.610
royal family, they spend about $2 billion
every year in order to keep up these sumptuous

00:09:35.610 --> 00:09:36.610
lifestyles.

00:09:36.610 --> 00:09:43.000
AUDIO: (But some other estimations indicate
the royal family takes over 1 million oil

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:45.350
barrels a day, that is 10% of the national
production.)

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:50.920
THE PROGRESS OF SAUDI VISION 2030

00:09:50.920 --> 00:09:57.380
Despite all of this, the transformation of
Saudi Arabia planned in Vision 2030 keeps

00:09:57.380 --> 00:09:58.380
moving forward.

00:09:58.380 --> 00:10:04.240
AUDIO: (“Saudi Arabia designs a city of
entertainment almost as big as Las Vegas”)

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:06.430
- The Independent
But the truth is it is moving slowly...

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:09.000
&nbsp;
And for the time being, Saudi Arabia is regaining

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:10.820
better relations with the US.

00:10:10.820 --> 00:10:15.320
In fact, Donald Trump’s first international
trip as the US president was to Riyadh.

00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:20.250
But yes, in order to achieve that the Saudis
had to sign some big cheques.

00:10:20.250 --> 00:10:25.620
AUDIO: (“Trump Signs "Single Largest Arms
Deal In US History" With Saudi Arabia Worth

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:30.100
$350 Billion” CNN)
This has to be added to the billion dollar

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:34.510
contracts they already have with the largest
companies in the United States.

00:10:34.510 --> 00:10:39.649
It all has a target in mind: Saudi Arabia
wants to reinforce the protection it has from

00:10:39.649 --> 00:10:42.550
the US to defend from possible enemies such
as Iran.

00:10:42.550 --> 00:10:46.620
We’re actually going to be discussing this
special relationship in a future video, so

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:47.850
don’t forget to subscribe!

00:10:47.850 --> 00:10:50.380
&nbsp;
But, leaving the US aside, in the last few

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:55.230
months, Saudi Arabia has set the world’s
largest fund for technological investment.

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:58.679
They have $100 billion available to invest.

00:10:58.679 --> 00:11:00.320
&nbsp;
Furthermore, the country is eliminating many

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:04.520
restrictions on foreign investment and some
projects are being discussed.

00:11:04.520 --> 00:11:08.810
Some of these have already been put into motion
such as theme parks, huge hotel resorts and,

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:11.430
even, nuclear power plants.

00:11:11.430 --> 00:11:15.200
&nbsp;
But as we have been telling you…transforming

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:20.860
this country won't be easy at all, and this
is just the start of their very own soap opera.

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:23.700
There’s the huge wasting of money from the
Royal family, which means they have to deal

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:28.080
with a lot of criticism from the country's
powerful religious leaders (who have a terrible

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:32.240
lack of respect for civil rights), then there
is the war in Yemen, and the uncertainty of

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:33.480
the heir of the Saudi throne.

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:37.860
So, now, what do you think about the luxurious
lifestyle of the Saudi royal family?

00:11:37.860 --> 00:11:41.300
Do you think Riyadh will ever become some
kind of Dubai?

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:46.029
Well, please leave your answers in the comments
below and click like if you enjoyed this video!

00:11:46.029 --> 00:11:51.040
And don’t forget to subscribe for brand
new videos every Monday and Thursday, and

00:11:51.040 --> 00:12:03.550
as always, I’ll see you next time!

